          If you are not certain whether a record is filed with the Leominster City Clerk, call the office for   confirmation at 978-534-7500 Option #3 before ordering. It is helpful if you provide us with a    telephone number when ordering so we may contact you with any questions. Birth Certificates The City Clerk’s Office is responsible for original records of all births that have occurred at Leominster Hospital or elsewhere within Leominster. Births occurring elsewhere in Massachusetts may also be on file here if the parents were residing in Leominster at the time of the birth. The fee for each certified copy is $10.00. A record is  not  accessible to the general public if the parents were unmarried at the time the child was born (and have not since married and amended the birth record), or if the father’s name does not appear on the record. When this is true, only the mother, father (if listed) or child may request a certificate. Identification will be required. If so, you can fax or email us a copy of the identification. Identification is not required for other records. Order Birth Certificate Online Birth-Certificate-Request-Form-Fillable Marriage Intentions/Certificates Step 1.  A marriage intention must be completed by both parties. The form must be typed or written in BLACK INK ONLY. All information needs to be filled in EXCEPT the signatures. This is needs to be done in the presence of the City Clerk's office. Once the paperwork is filled out , it will need to be brought to the City Clerk's office with both parties present and both will need to provide proof of age such as a certified birth certificate, passport or Real ID. (a driver's license that is not a real id is not sufficient) This form is available online. The fee to file the intention is $30.00, payable by cash , card, or check. There will be a $2.95 processing fee added if paying with a debit or credit card. Step 2.  There is a 3-day waiting period before you can pick up your marriage license, that pick up day will be told to the both of you at the City Clerk's office. The license is good for 60 days. If you are not married within 60 days of the date the license was granted, you will need to apply all over again. Step 3.  After the 3-day waiting period, come to the City Clerk's office and pick up your marriage license which will be given to the officiant that is marrying you. They will fill out and sign  Section #20 ONLY-with black ink. Step 4.  Return the marriage license to the City Clerk's office. The marriage certificate must be returned to the City Clerk's office within 60 day window. If a copy of the marriage is needed, the fee foe each certified copy is $10.00, payable by cash, credit, or check. Marriage certificates that are needed after marriage, can be obtained in the city or town where the couple applied for the marriage license and not where the couple got married. If you applied for a marriage license in Leominster, you can obtain a certified Marriage Certificate here after the wedding takes place. The fee for each certified copy is $10.00. Order Marriage Certificate Online .  Getting-Married-Information /DocumentCenter/View/4062/Marriage-Intention-Packet-FILLABLE Death Certificates The City Clerk’s Office is responsible for original records of all deaths that have occurred in Leominster, including Leominster Hospital. Death certificates can only be issued for individuals who lived in Leominster at the time of passing. All death certificates are public records. A certified copy of a death certificate may be obtained in person, online or by mail. ***Please be advised that as of July 1, 2026 social security numbers will NO LONGER be made available on death certificates in accordance with the amended law,  M.G.L. c. 46, § 1.*** If this is needed, a request MUST be made ahead of time through the City Clerk's Office.  The fee for each certified copy is $10.00.   Order Death Certificate Online   /DocumentCenter/View/3684/Marriage-and-Death-Form-Fillable Business Licenses If the applicant is applying for a home business; they must either be the homeowner or have a letter from the landlord stating that they are allowed to have a business in the home. A home office means that there are no customers or deliveries coming to the home and only one commercial vehicle is allowed on the property. If the applicant is applying for a business license and has obtained space outside of the home they must bring a copy of their signed lease, or a letter from the building owner stating that they are a tenant in the building. Business Certificate Application (DBA) Dog Licenses You are no longer able to process your dog licenses online. You can either mail in the application below along with a current rabies certificate, a check or money order made payable to the City of Leominster for $10.00 if the dog is spayed/neutered, $15.00 if the dog is not altered as well as a self addressed , stamp envelope. You may also come into the City Clerk's office during normal business hours. We accept cash, check, credit card or money order. Please be aware that there is a $2.95 processing fee for using a credit card. Please contact us at 978-534-7500 Option #3 or  Email City Clerk Department  with any questions or concerns. No licensing fee will be assessed for any dogs owned by individuals ages 70 or older.  Proof of age, such as a copy of a Driver's License or Birth Certificate must be provided. /DocumentCenter/View/3657/Dog-License-Mail-In-Application 
     

 
